        {
          "page_number": 2,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "level": 1,
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Basic probability"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "level": 2,
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "What is probability?"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet_list",
              "items": [
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Probability describes the likelihood of something happening"
                    }
                  ],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "In real-life you might use words such as impossible, unlikely and certain"
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "In maths we use the probability scale to describe probability"
                    }
                  ],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "This means giving it a number between "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "math",
                          "latex": "0"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " and "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "math",
                          "latex": "1"
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "math",
                              "latex": "0"
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " means impossible"
                            }
                          ],
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Between "
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "math",
                              "latex": "0"
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " and "
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "math",
                              "latex": "0.5"
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " means unlikely"
                            }
                          ],
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "math",
                              "latex": "0.5"
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " means even chance"
                            }
                          ],
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Between "
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "math",
                              "latex": "0.5"
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " and "
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "math",
                              "latex": "1"
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " means likely"
                            }
                          ],
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "math",
                              "latex": "1"
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " means certain"
                            }
                          ],
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Probabilities can be given as fractions, decimals or percentages"
                    }
                  ],
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "figure_type": "diagram",
              "description": "A probability scale drawn as a horizontal number line running from 0 to 1 with evenly spaced tick marks. Curly braces and arrows connect regions of the scale to labelled boxes: Impossible at 0, Unlikely between 0 and 0.5, Even chance at 0.5, Likely between 0.5 and 1, and Certain at 1. Illustrations above the scale include a flying pig, a dice, a coin, a spinner, and a sun with a crescent moon and stars.",
              "caption": "Probability scale",
              "needs_asset_extraction": true
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "level": 2,
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "What key words and terminology are used in probability?"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet_list",
              "items": [
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "An experiment is an activity that is repeated to produce a set of results"
                    }
                  ],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Results can be observed (seen) or recorded"
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Each repeat is called a trial"
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "An outcome is a possible result of a trial"
                    }
                  ],
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "page_number": 3,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet_list",
              "items": [
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "An event is an outcome (or a collection of outcomes)"
                    }
                  ],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "For example:"
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "a dice lands on a six"
                            }
                          ],
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "a dice lands on an even number"
                            }
                          ],
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Events are usually given capital letters"
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "math",
                          "latex": "n(A)"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " is the number of possible outcomes from event "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "math",
                          "latex": "A"
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "math",
                              "latex": "A"
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " = a dice lands on an even number (2, 4 or 6)"
                            }
                          ],
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "math",
                              "latex": "n(A) = 3"
                            }
                          ],
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "A sample space is the set of all possible outcomes of an experiment"
                    }
                  ],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "It can be represented as a list or a table"
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The probability of event "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "math",
                      "latex": "A"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " is written "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "math",
                      "latex": "\\mathrm{P}(A)"
                    }
                  ],
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "An event is said to be fair if there is an equal chance of achieving each outcome"
                    }
                  ],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "If there is not an equal chance, the event is biased"
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "For example, a fair coin has an equal chance of landing on heads or tails"
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "level": 2,
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "How do I calculate basic probabilities?"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet_list",
              "items": [
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "If all outcomes are equally likely then the probability for each outcome is the same"
                    }
                  ],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "The probability for each outcome is "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "math",
                          "latex": "\\frac{1}{\\text{Total number of outcomes}}"
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "If there are 50 marbles in a bag then the probability of selecting a specific one is "
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "math",
                              "latex": "\\frac{1}{50}"
                            }
                          ],
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The theoretical probability of an event can be calculated by dividing the number of outcomes of that event by the total number of outcomes"
                    }
                  ],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "math",
                          "latex": "\\mathrm{P}(A) = \\frac{\\text{Total number of outcomes for the event}}{\\text{Total number of outcomes}}"
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "This can be calculated without actually doing the experiment"
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "If there are 50 marbles in a bag and 20 are blue, then the probability of selecting a blue marble is "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "math",
                      "latex": "\\frac{20}{50}"
                    }
                  ],
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "level": 2,
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "How do I find missing probabilities?"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet_list",
              "items": [
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The probabilities of all the outcomes add up to 1"
                    }
                  ],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "If you have a table of probabilities with one missing, find it by making them all add up to 1"
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The complement of event "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "math",
                      "latex": "A"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " is the event where "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "math",
                      "latex": "A"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " does not happen"
                    }
                  ],
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "page_number": 4,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet_list",
              "items": [
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "This can be thought of as not "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "math",
                      "latex": "A"
                    }
                  ],
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "math",
                      "latex": "\\text{P(event does not happen)} = 1 - \\text{P(event does happen)}"
                    }
                  ],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "For example, if the probability of rain is "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "math",
                          "latex": "0.3"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": ", then the probability of not rain is "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "math",
                          "latex": "1 - 0.3 = 0.7"
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "level": 2,
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "What are mutually exclusive events?"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet_list",
              "items": [
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Two events are mutually exclusive if they cannot both happen at once"
                    }
                  ],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "When rolling a dice, the events “getting a prime number” and “getting a 6” are mutually exclusive (as 6 is not prime)"
                        }
                      ],
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "If "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "math",
                      "latex": "A"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " and "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "math",
                      "latex": "B"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " are mutually exclusive events, then the probability of either A or B happening is "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "math",
                      "latex": "P(A) + P(B)"
                    }
                  ],
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Complementary events are mutually exclusive"
                    }
                  ],
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "level": 3,
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Examiner Tips and Tricks"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "If you are not told in the question how to leave your answer, then fractions are best for probabilities."
                }
